1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,900
Welcome to Island Time. This tutorial shows you how to play, from your first morning to the end of your stay.

2
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:15,450
Island Time is about living on Anderson Island, in the south of Puget Sound.

3
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:24,229
There’s no bridge. One small county ferry connects you to work, groceries, gas and doctors.

4
00:00:24,229 --> 00:00:31,379
From the title screen you can start a new life on the island, visit it, or try a challenge.

5
00:00:31,379 --> 00:00:35,919
Start by telling your neighbors what to call you.

6
00:00:35,919 --> 00:00:40,429
You can change your name any time in Settings.

7
00:00:40,429 --> 00:00:48,129
Then pick a difficulty. Islander is forgiving, and Normal is the game as designed.

8
00:00:48,129 --> 00:00:55,330
Ferry Hell brings summer crowds, constant breakdowns, weekly rent and car trouble.

9
00:00:55,330 --> 00:01:01,949
Next you choose a week, a month, or a whole year in story mode, and a season.

10
00:01:01,949 --> 00:01:10,330
At the top are the day, the time, and six numbers: cash, food, health, stress, job and home.

11
00:01:10,330 --> 00:01:17,870
Food is the days of groceries in your pantry. Health and stress follow how your days go.

12
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:23,820
The Next up card always shows the one thing that matters most right now.

13
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:29,700
Below that is everything you can do where you are, grouped into sections.

14
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:36,230
Every action takes time on the clock, and most of them cost or earn something.

15
00:01:36,230 --> 00:01:43,210
Open Go somewhere to travel. You can switch between a list and a real map.

16
00:01:43,210 --> 00:01:49,590
Tap a place to see how to get there: drive, walk, or ride with a neighbor.

17
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:55,130
The Ferry tab shows every sailing, and has a trip planner.

18
00:01:55,130 --> 00:02:01,730
Tell it where you need to be and when, and it tells you which boat to catch and when to leave.

19
00:02:01,730 --> 00:02:07,630
At the landing, get in line about twenty minutes before the boat leaves.

20
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:15,260
Boats fill up at rush hour. If you’re too far back in line, you wait for the next one.

21
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:21,740
Crew shortages, breakdowns, fog and storms can cancel sailings.

22
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:28,100
Rider alerts warn you, and the boats right after an outage fill up fast.

23
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:34,750
Miss the last boat home, and you’ll need a motel, a friend’s couch, or your car.

24
00:02:34,750 --> 00:02:39,960
Your job is in Lakewood, and your shift starts at nine.

25
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:47,660
Late arrivals and missed days lower your Job meter. Let it fall too far and you’re fired.

26
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:52,580
You can always look for new work in the job listings.

27
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:58,890
Bills arrive by mail: power, internet, phone and insurance.

28
00:02:58,890 --> 00:03:07,240
The credit union app shows what you owe. When cash runs out, essentials can go on your card.

29
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:13,550
The island’s only store has closed, so groceries come from the mainland.

30
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:21,090
Buy food in Lakewood and keep the pantry stocked. You eat a day of food every night.

31
00:03:21,090 --> 00:03:27,090
There’s no gas station on the island either, so fill up on the mainland.

32
00:03:27,090 --> 00:03:35,730
Gas cans aren’t allowed on the ferry. In a pinch, Dale sells gas by the gallon, for a price.

33
00:03:35,730 --> 00:03:42,500
Your phone has messages, calls, an alarm clock, and five apps you choose.

34
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:49,680
Ferry alerts, the weather, rides, the credit union and the Island Group are all useful.

35
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:56,090
The island only gets one bar of signal, so installs and calls are slow.

36
00:03:56,090 --> 00:04:03,310
The Island Group is the community board. Ask for help there, or help others.

37
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:09,650
Helping neighbors builds your reputation, and friends do favors in return.

38
00:04:09,650 --> 00:04:16,300
The To-do tab tracks your shifts, appointments, bills and repairs for the week.

39
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:21,030
Pin your own priorities, so nothing slips.

40
00:04:21,030 --> 00:04:27,890
Your cabin needs care. Chores and repairs keep the Home meter up.

41
00:04:27,890 --> 00:04:34,130
Ignored jobs turn into floods, leaks and mice, so check what’s due.

42
00:04:34,130 --> 00:04:41,790
The Your vehicles card shows each car and your boat: where it is, its fuel, battery and tires.

43
00:04:41,790 --> 00:04:48,610
Each car has its own parts, so a weak battery on one doesn’t affect the others.

44
00:04:48,610 --> 00:04:54,470
Buy a skiff, and cross on your own schedule when the water is calm.

45
00:04:54,470 --> 00:05:01,380
Keep it in a slip at the marina, on a trailer in your yard, or on a buoy off your beach.

46
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:06,300
Each night you go to bed and see a summary of your day.

47
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:12,350
Set your alarms first, so you don’t oversleep and miss the morning boat.

48
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:19,980
Visitor mode flips the game: you live on the mainland and visit for a day, a weekend or a week.

49
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:26,290
See the sights, spend your budget wisely, and catch the last boat home.

50
00:05:26,290 --> 00:05:32,750
As a weekend regular, you work in the city and spend your weekends on the island.

51
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:38,890
Save up and make friends, and you might be able to buy a house and move over.

52
00:05:38,890 --> 00:05:43,830
At the end you get a score and a summary of your stay.

53
00:05:43,830 --> 00:05:49,640
Then try a harder level, a different season, or the story mode.

54
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:56,070
After each update, the What’s new button on the title screen shows what changed.

55
00:05:56,070 --> 00:06:00,630
You can watch this tutorial there any time.

56
00:06:00,630 --> 00:06:10,850
That’s everything you need. Welcome to the island! Play free at krazow.github.io/islandtime

